      "body": "## Overview\n\nThe Mooncake connector tests mock the bootstrap HTTP client by patching the top-level `httpx` module. Since #56460 the connector imports `httpx` from `huggingface_hub.utils`, which `huggingface_hub` 2.x resolves to `httpx2`. With hub 2.x installed, those mocks never take effect.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `test_register_worker_retries_on_read_timeout` and `test_register_worker_raises_after_max_attempts` pass with `huggingface_hub` 2.x; they currently fail there.\n- Behavior under the CI pin (`huggingface-hub==1.31.0`) is unchanged: there, `huggingface_hub.utils.httpx` is the same top-level `httpx` the tests patched before.\n\n## Validation\n\n`pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_connector.py` in an environment with `huggingface_hub` 2.2.0, `httpx2` 2.13.1 and `httpx` 0.28.1:\n\n| | register_worker tests | whole file |\n|---|---|---|\n| main | 2 failed: `assert 0 == 3` (the stub client is never called), then real connection attempts | n/a |\n| this PR | passed | 123 passed |\n\n## Details\n\n- **Root cause:**\n  - `mooncake_connector.py` does `from huggingface_hub.utils import httpx`.\n  - In `huggingface_hub` 1.x, `utils/__init__.py` does `import httpx`, with a comment that it \"will be httpx2 in huggingface_hub v2.x\". In 2.x, `utils.__getattr__(\"httpx\")` returns `importlib.import_module(\"httpx2\")`.\n  - The tests did `import httpx` and patched `httpx.AsyncClient`, which is a different module object from the connector's under 2.x. The real `httpx2` client ran instead: no calls were recorded, and the retry test exhausted its attempts against a host that doesn't exist.\n  - `_FlakyAsyncClient` raised the top-level `httpx.ReadTimeout`, which the connector's `except httpx.TimeoutException` (an `httpx2` class under 2.x) would not catch either.\n- **Fix:** the test module now imports `httpx` exactly as the connector does. Every patch, and the stub's exception, then refers to the connector's module under either hub version.\n  - `patch_worker_dependencies` switches from `patch(\"httpx.AsyncClient\")` to `patch.object(httpx, \"AsyncClient\")` for the same reason.\n  - Tests that open a real client against the local bootstrap server now use that same module, which works under either version.\n- **CI coverage:** CI's pinned hub 1.31.0 doesn't exercise the failure, so this was validated locally with hub 2.2.0.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nThis PR was written with AI assistance (Claude); I reviewed every line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
